## 47. Book 6 ch49 — the certification minute's "evaluator of record" (coordinator ruling, 2026-10-11)
The protected Tier B minute reads "*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*" In this edition Gault is the evaluator of record and the Archmarshal's office is the certifying office that declined. **Ruling: the protected line stays verbatim and is read as the form's own mislabel** — an old column heading with no place for the right office — which the scene already dramatizes (four pens stop; Gault "had declined nothing"). One plain sentence was added outside the protected line so a young reader is told so directly: "The refusal was the Archmarshal's; the form's old column had only Gault's title to put it under." Owner may instead release the protected line and have it name the certifying office.

## 48. Book 7 reconciliation to edition Book 6 (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
Source: `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md`, `B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md` (Sol) and `B6-RECONCILIATION-COORDINATOR-OVERRIDES.md`. Defaults in force until the owner rules:
- **Season-blind and feet/yards, continued into Book 7** (as #37 O1 and #42 did for Books 5 and 6). Named seasons and metric units are replaced, minimally, INCLUDING inside Book 7's protected lines (for example "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." becomes "After the thaw. …"; "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." becomes the same distance in yards). Generic "season" and "month" stay. Every changed protected line is listed, old and new, in `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md`; the owner may restore any or all when the series calendar is ruled.
- **Time since Kindling** (#18 extended to Book 7): the protected first pole "I've spent four years being the case the instruments couldn't parse" reads "Since my Kindling I've been the case…".
- **The birthday:** day 102 past the Line stands, never beside a season, a month order or a count back to the last birthday. By the edition's own day counts the two birthdays fall roughly 225 days apart (Book 6's mid-year, the year's close near day 207, then 102 days). The prose never states it; the series calendar remains the owner's to rule (#35, #42).
- **The shelf** is the second camp past the Line and the first fire (#46). **The Velmere letter** stays sealed on Brom's table at Halcenvane; it is not carried. **Seln's case** came east in his own satchel and rides under the canvas from the shelf.
- **Shadow's first Book 7 use** is restaged so Oryn cannot see or attribute it (audit B2). **#23** (sell the cart and gelding in Lowmarch's first week; the money is a sealed reserve) is treated as binding.

## 49. Book 7 — protected Quiet-line / Kindling wording (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 4)
Seven protected lines say variants of "mine didn't", "my Path", "mine has been asleep since I was fourteen", "dark since fourteen", "every Path … his had not". Edition canon (Book 6): Cael's own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and the Arbiter went dark; he has no Path. At a Quiet line the others' live Arbiters stop, his is dark before and after, and his fragments still answer. **Default until ruled: the protected lines stay verbatim**, the surrounding plan and prose state the canon, and the lines read as Cael's own shorthand. Options: (1) release only the conflicting clauses for a minimal canon repair; (2) release the affected log entries for clean re-composition; (3) keep as is (the default).

**#49 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 4).** Read closely, most of the seven lines already agree with canon as written: the first says the others' ARBITERS stopped and "Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen."; the fourth says "whatever I am isn't a Path"; Karis's struck line says "one dark since fourteen; no change either side of the line". Only two use "Path … mine" loosely ("Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't"; "every Path in this camp stops, and mine doesn't"). Default confirmed: all seven stay verbatim as Cael's log shorthand; Movement 4's packet carries a binding note that narration and dialogue never say "his Path" and state the canon exactly (the five live Arbiters stop; his has been dark since Kindling; the fragments still answer). If the owner prefers, only those two clauses need releasing.

## 50. Book 7 — "Six years I've wanted a face" (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 7)
The protected line gives Seln six years; edition Book 6 has him carry the case twelve years (fifteen in service). **Default until ruled: the line stays verbatim** and the plan stops calling the case a six-year matter. Options: (1) "Twelve years I've wanted a face."; (2) "All these years I've wanted a face."; (3) keep six and name a separate event six years back that began the wish.

**#50 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 7).** Default confirmed and written into Movement 7's packet: the line stays verbatim and unglossed; no six-year event is invented; the case's twelve years is not stated in that scene. One thing the owner may like to know: the closed Movement 5 has Seln date the registry's survey of the circles at "five years ago by the stake, maybe six" (ch34), so on the page "six years" can be heard as the time since that survey without any change. If the owner prefers option (1) or (2), it is a one-numeral change.

## 51. Book 7 — "Tomorrow makes three" (OWNER ITEM; coordinator default in force, 2026-10-11)
The protected second pole closes Movement 6 (ch44, written at the well as day 111 breaks): "…We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." On this edition's calendar "tomorrow" is day 112, a road to Lowmarch's board; the next quiet ground entered is the Stair on day 114. The count is also arguable: the six have gone in at the Fallow once as a party (day 96), or twice if the first crossings at the line are counted. Sol's audit found no honest gloss. **Default until ruled: the line stays word for word, where the plan places it, unglossed.** Options: (1) keep as is (the default); (2) keep the words and move the entry to the night of day 113, the eve of the Stair, where "tomorrow" is true (Movement 6 would then close on Oryn's leaving); (3) supply replacement wording. Options 2 and 3 change published chapters.
- Related, NOT an owner item: the restored protected line "I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board" beside Oryn at Millrace (one day south of Lowmarch) on day 113 was resolved by the owner on 2026-09-04 (EXC-B7-003: "her circuit brings her round to the Stair-road stop within three days"; BOOK_MAP lists it under "do not reopen"). Movement 7's packet carries a binding note.

