    84	
    85	He lay and counted them, and there were nine. It was like a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on. Every stick in it was where he had always known that it was. He had crossed that floor ten thousand times in the dark without barking a shin; and he had never once seen it.
    86	
    87	"How many people."
    88	
    89	It came from the ladder's head, quite low. Brom was sitting there with his back against a sack and his legs hanging into the barn, and he had plainly been there for some time.
    90	
    91	Cael sat up.
    92	
    93	"Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with."
    94	
