   150	
   151	"You're walking like the carter," said Lira. "The one with the feet."
   152	
   153	She had left off counting sacks. She was watching him come away from the well, a stride at a time, with the look that she had worn at the rail of a practice floor.
   154	
   155	"The ground's late."
