   295	He slept that night for four hours together, which was four more than the night before. The nine were all there when he woke in the dark, each in its place, with a wall of barley standing over them; and he let them be nine without going along the row. A forge was a forge. The low sound lay where it had lain down at noon, and the boards under his back came to him almost when they should.

