   212	
   213	"That's it," said Oryn.
   214	
   215	She slung the pannier on her back and went to the mule, and laid her hand once on the brown neck. Then she walked away across the yard toward the northern fence, on the low side of nothing, and she went through the wicket without a glance behind her.
   216	
