editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-55.md-226-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-55.md-227-"You're going to tell me about a thing that I'll never get my hands on. I'd take a finding from a second healer across a table, if I had felt the patient. I've not felt this one. I've had a river in the dark off you seven times, and that's all that I'll ever have." She spoke slowly, sorting it. "But you were in me for a minute, on that ridge, and I felt you go along. I know your step. If you're in me while you say it, I'll have the thing that found it, under my own skin, while it tells me what it found. It's the nearest that I'll come."
