editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-40.md-309-The steading's woman cleared the board herself. She took six bowls on one arm, and left what was not hers to clear: a basket with three brown apples in it, and a book, and a scrap of bark. Cael drew Hesk's satchel up from under the bench to put the bark away with Pike's other lines.
