editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/pre-lanes/chapter-40.md-311-That satchel had been a parcel once. It had come to him in oilcloth on the last of these days, tied with a knot that undid at one pull for anybody who knew the end of it; and a leaf from an order-pad lay under its flap still, folded small. He knew before he looked that there was nothing beside the leaf tonight. No boat had come in from the west since the ninety-first day, and a carter cannot bring up a valley what a ferry has not landed.
