176:**Vocabulary** (this series' own): fragment, notice, integration, acquisition (directed), engagement (clinical — non-hostile), Path, declaration, tier, rank, Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver/Gold, Arbiter, sigil, idle state, deployment, the hold, discharge, the reading (surface / deep), mending, reserve, the line, quiet ground → the Quieting, perimeter, radius, stake, the board, HOLD, outcome, the wall. The system's voices are the **log** (Cael's inventory), the **notice** (one only, the tenth), and **Pike's ledger lines**. Interface text appears only where the canon calls for it.
180:**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
188:| **Shadow-adjacent** (sealed) | Drifts at dusk in M1–M4 and is held. **Used exactly twice:** M5 ten strides to reach Karis (the informed B6 circle only; Oryn cannot see or attribute the use) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2]; M7 up the stair and across the bowl, unseen by the rim, never attributable | Costs from waking; the seal's whole logic is restated once (M2 log) and honored |
192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
196:**Others' progression:** Lira learns to be fast with nothing at the end (M2), and learns to shoot braced one-armed (M6 → M8). Brom learns Iron Skin is a shout out here, and what he is without it ("a big man with good footwork and a lip of fused stone"). Karis learns to keep one point; the lattice line across a mountain; the wall along a line from her knees. Seln learns that his Path "was never most of what I do." Oryn: what her hands can and cannot do at a line, tested eight times alone. Teague: a column he does not have.
206:| M1 | The Thornwater stretch at dusk: a mile with a grey shape at forty-five yards, nobody declaring [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] | 3,500–4,000 | Tension set piece; no blow struck |
222:**Injuries tracked forward (no silent healing):** Cael's calf (53 → reopened 78 and 96 → closed 99); ribs (78 → taped 81 → off 99 → the Hall's bill 119 → cold-aggravated 123 → quiet at 129). Lira's right ankle (53, 78, 96; **never mended**); her leg (broken 78, mended 80); her left forearm (96 → season order → reopened 114 → closed; slung at 131). Brom's forearm (53 → reopened 78 → mended 80); his hand (96 → mended 97); his shoulder (114 → mended; reopened 119 → mended twice → bound 120). Karis's palms (53, scars); empty (78); throat and voice (96 → mended 97, voice back by ~110). Seln: unmarked. Oryn: drained at every mending, priced aloud.
232:**The source's refrains:** Read the source for events, not sentences. It leans on a handful of refrains: "catalogued," "which was a ledger line," "which from Seln was a whole report," "a stride and a half," "the voice for a distance / an inventory," "filed," "the shelf," "did not have a column for it," and "which was, from X, a paragraph." Keep a few as character signatures (Cael catalogues; Pike reads things twice; a stride and a half is Oryn's distance). Thin the rest hard. Protected lines (§10) are exempt.
234:**Reader Standard (outranks voice):** clean language, moral clarity, violence with cost and no gore, no innuendo. Carry the source's Gate-27 WATCH notes into the retelling. The ford witness who "got his hand across his own throat somehow" must read unambiguously as *not* self-inflicted (he got his hand between the jaws and his throat). Name the den's remains in one clause. Blood once, as stakes. Cael's decision to read Oryn without consent is named as wrong by him and by three others before it happens.
240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's after-thaw term [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
243:- Pike's Thornwater-road line (Ch1): *Thornwater road, the stretch. Walked ahead of one cart, one carter, one mule. Delivered at the fence. No losses. Nine marks, paid.*
244:- Pike's ford line (Ch3–4): *Stillhound pack, Thornwater ford: cleared. Five confirmed. Crew of five, four injured, none lost. Price paid.*
245:- Pike's traverse line (Ch8): "High traverse, Oxhollow to Thornwater. Mapped. Delivered at the ford. Carts go round." … "Cart lost. Crew of five, three hurt, none lost. Seventy." … *less six, the cart.* — "Seventy's what the ford paid. Sixty-four's what the job was worth. That's what goes on the wall."
246:- The Fallow slip (Ch8, Ch12): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Fallow road. East of Thornwater; the second day; where the road leaves its line at the rise and comes back to it. One hundred marks (one hundred).* Seal: a hook and a bar, in dark wax.
247:- Pike's Fallow copy (Ch14; read again Ch17): *Recovery, Fallow road, broker's posting. Taken. Witnessed. Completed: incomplete — instruments not recovered — crew returned. Six went in. Six came out. No price paid.*
248:- The Stair slip (Ch17): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Stair road. South of Lowmarch; the first day; where the road drops off the ridge and the ground opens. Three hundred marks (three hundred).*
259:- Pike's season line (Ch24): "*Crew of six. Ford cleared, traverse mapped, Ring entered, Stair entered and instruments recovered, Hall entered. No losses. Returned every time.*" — and the Stair's price column: *three hundred; taken; not paid*.
260:- The Vastin window (Ch16), substance exact, three sentences: Vastin received the broker's completion report as a courtesy copy, forwarded through a registry office that had no interest in any board east of the Line, in the second folder of the morning, marked *Fallow Ring: crew returned, instruments not recovered*. He read it twice — a broker's report from a town on no registry map, on his desk with no routing note — and did not know why it had reached him, and filed that, in the register of a man who had never once in forty years pretended to knowledge he lacked, as the whole of what he knew about it. He returned the copy to its folder unannotated.
265:- Vell (Ch9): *Filed with your record. It reads: left in good standing, undefeated on paper. I've kept this ledger forty years and never had a line like it. The session still stands. The road still runs through Ardenmere. — V.*
269:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
277:- Ch7: *Teague priced us. He's right about the cart. Oryn read me three times and got nothing three times and wants a fourth. Two people out here measuring me, and neither of them has a seal. I keep waiting to mind.*
278:- Ch8, Part-1 summary (EXC-B7-001): *Twelve weeks. Seven contracts. Pike says there's ground out here where the Arbiter goes quiet, and nobody goes in twice. Karis has been waiting her whole life for a sentence like that. Seln says the contract was written by someone from inside. I say it pays. Two days east, through Thornwater, on the day the healer said. For twelve weeks nothing out here has read me. I'd like to see what a place that reads nothing does with that.*
279:- Ch9, at the stone: *Quiet ground. Karis's Arbiter stopped at a line she can mark with a rock. So did Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's — same line, same step. Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen. I don't know what that means. Nobody asked. Tomorrow we go in.* [OWNER-pending #49]
280:- Ch10: *The circle is perfect. The stakes are the registry's. The dogs are inside. Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't, and I've told nobody, and I'm going to need to think about why I haven't. Not tonight. Tonight we're inside the one place on the continent where a stillhound can't lose.* [OWNER-pending #49]
283:- Ch13, the covenant, whole: *Written before. Tomorrow morning, the back room, the door shut. Oryn runs the long reading. Both hands, all of her, all of me, twenty minutes. I lie still. I'm still and whole for the first time in front of her; she said so in the yard, with the tape off.* / *The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.* / *The price. She doesn't know what I am. She can't consent to what she can't know about — not won't; can't. There's nothing I could put in front of her tonight that she could say yes or no to, because the thing doesn't have a name she's heard. I've decided not to tell her before. My reasons are good, and they're the reasons of somebody who wants it, and the real one is that I don't know what she'd say. Entered.* / *If it takes what she's using on me, it takes it from the one person on this road who came to help. I don't know what it costs a source. It's never shown. Tomorrow's the first time it could, and if it does, she pays, and I chose that for her.* / *After: I tell her. In full. On her table, before I'm off it. Whatever it costs me, including the route walking north without me on it.* / *I want it. Write that too.* / *Write it before, not after. That's the whole difference between me and the system.*
284:- Ch14, the birthday line: *Hundred and second day past the Line. Nineteen. Written at Thornwater, in the steading's common room, the fire lit for us. Witnesses: four of my own, and a healer who's a stop.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
285:- Ch14, the words retired: *Still open. Still real. Now I can see it. That's worse. The tenth fragment lets me feel my own currents, and there's one in the place session nine logged, and it isn't the tenth, and it isn't any of the nine. It was there before Oryn. It was there before Brom's read caught it. I don't know what it is. I know where it is now. Patience is over; observation begins.* — and *Daeva's rematch, Reydan's answer — both ride east. Nineteen. Ten fragments. Hesk's package is on a ferry somewhere. The last one said mind the shape. I'm starting to.*
287:- Ch16, the second pole: *Nothing out here reads me. And at a line you can mark with a rock, every Path in this camp stops, and mine doesn't. Karis won't write her hypothesis. I won't write mine. We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three.* [OWNER-pending #49]
289:- Ch18: *Hundred and thirteenth day, the fork above Millrace. Oryn came. On her terms. She'll turn north the day she has to and I won't ask her not to.*
291:- Ch20: *Instruments recovered. The contract's paid, and the man who posted it is never going to see them, because Seln's keeping the ledger and I'm keeping the kit. Someone measured this place five years ago and wrote bearing and stopped. Karis has a straightedge. She's been waiting her whole life to use it. The Ring, the Stair, and whatever's on that bearing. Pike said a handful. We have two. The kit says three. We're going to go look.*
292:- Ch22, the still place: *Read myself. Ten currents, and I can't find the banks either — Oryn's right. And the anomaly's there. Not a fragment. Not a flow. A still place, and the rest of me has been going around it since before I knew it existed. It isn't the Quiet. The Quiet is outside me and turns Paths off. This is inside me and the Paths — the fragments — go around it like they were built to. I don't know what it is. I know it was there before Oryn, before Brom's read, before the ring. Session nine caught the edge of it. I'm not going to guess. Guessing is what the registry did to me. Observation, then the log, then patience.*
293:- Ch22, the stake paid: *Teague sat down next to me. Asked what I am. I could have read him. I asked instead. The day I stop asking is the day I'm the registry. Write it down. Again. Every time.*
294:- Ch23: *Hundred and twenty-second day, the fork. Oryn north. On her terms. I didn't ask. Five on the bearing.* — *I love this country.* — and the crest: *Four sites. One line. The last one's twice the size and the Compact fenced it. The bearing runs through it and keeps going. Karis says four points is an argument. I say it's a bearing — the kind their maps draw as nothing. Home is Lowmarch now. I just wrote that without noticing. Nineteen, ten fragments, a still place at the center of me, and a line on a map that somebody drew before there were maps. We're not done. We're oriented.*
295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
298:- Ch1: "You're paper, aren't you" … "Then you know how to keep quiet. Keep it." — Seln: "Don't declare anything." — Lira: "I could clear it." / "No," said Seln. / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it." — The carter: "First crew I've hired that knew to shut up." — "Stillhound." … "It's a stillhound. You shut up. It went home."
299:- Ch2: Pike: "Once before it's in, so she can say it's wrong. Once after, so it's said." … "Half this meadow can't read. The book's for me. The saying's for them." — "A Bronze who lost my carter is worth less than a Copper who brought him home. Out here that's arithmetic. In there it was heresy." — Seln: "West of that, the inventory executes the hour any of us shows paper. Pending jurisdiction means armed. Nobody goes west." / Brom: "Nobody wants to." / Karis: "Nobody can. Different sentences." — Pike: "Four lines. Nobody lost, nobody hurt, nobody knows you."

