editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/LANE-RULINGS.md:10:## Lane B (ch31–60) — 140 edits, on the brief's numbers; −1,581 words
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/LANE-RULINGS.md:11:1. **Scope of the consent freeze:** ch36–38 were left whole; in ch47, 48, 55 and 56 the lane made thirteen narration-only edits outside the passages the whole-arc read cites. The coordinator read all thirteen. Eleven stand (tics, counted pauses, a stage beat inside a speech with the spoken words unchanged). **Two are restored to the baseline by the coordinator:** ch55, the sentence in which Cael understands what Oryn's reserve costs a child at some northern gate (substance, not a tic); and ch56, Teague's read of where the six lay (the cut left "such pains over what they leave behind" without its antecedent and dropped the directions they went).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/LANE-RULINGS.md:12:2. **ch41 (−249 words; 812 words a scene):** accepted. The whole-arc read asked for condensation on the research plateau; nothing is restored.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/LANE-RULINGS.md:13:3. **Probe:** Lane A's ruling 1 applies to the six denominator-only one-point ticks. Six recasts that moved a sentence nearer the source were restored by the lane itself.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:9:**PASS — RATIFY.** The book holds as a complete novel. It begins by making freedom from institutional measurement feel materially true: the board records deeds, not rank, and Cael can write `I'm free` without irony (ch7:27–103, :269–295). It then makes that freedom morally insufficient. Quiet ground turns his old absence into unique power (ch27:181–239; ch29:243–309), the Ring lets him become the only effective practitioner in the party (ch31:211–289; ch32:139–301), and he uses that advantage to take from Oryn without consent (ch36:65–225; ch37:141–240). The second half does not absolve him. It builds a rule through refusal, explicit permission, repayment and restraint (ch38:103–229; ch47:97–129; ch48:7–105; ch55:221–287; ch56:153–205). The ending therefore earns both claims at once: nobody out here can reduce him to an instrument, and the place where only he works still requires other people, their boundaries and their evidence (ch58:219–229; ch60:31–41, :247–265).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:17:The required dates are exact: shelf day 2 (ch1:3–7); Lowmarch day 9 (ch2:3); ford day 53 (ch9:317; ch10:3–9); mountain days 70–84 (ch15:1–7; ch22:323–331); Fallow days 94–96 (ch27:157–183; ch28:67–105; ch30:237); long reading day 100 (ch36:233–279; ch38:77–87); birthday day 102 (ch40:3–5, :189–209); Oryn north day 111 (ch44:225–261; ch45:3–15); Millrace day 113 (ch47:3–25, :121–153); Stair days 114–115 (ch49:3–19; ch52:3–21, :355–359); Hall day 119 (ch54:3–15; ch55:153–165); first snow day 129 (ch59:121–139; ch60:31); last ferry day 130 (ch60:47–95); Oryn's letter day 131 (ch60:219–225).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:25:The fragment mechanics do not drift. Iron reads air or body, never both (ch4:97); Storm lanes bill ten, ten and twelve and clear at eleven, eleven and thirteen (ch4:97; ch32:215; ch51:47); Wind locks the landing for one count (ch4:85; ch32:163; ch51:21–33); Anchor is sure at ten feet, faint at twelve and absent at fourteen (ch4:99; ch50:261–293); Compression acts at contact (ch4:91; ch51:51–59); Ember remains one point (ch32:47; ch51:73–83, :213); Blade remains partial (ch4:101); Tide remains self-and-contact and governed by the body's owner (ch38:39; ch48:17–23, :73–105; ch60:37).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:27:Shadow is used exactly twice, at the Ring and Stair (ch32:117–127; ch50:213–255). Both uses are outside hostile sight; Oryn sees neither and never learns Seln is the source (ch34:25–47; ch51:165–173). The closing inventory states the same sealed logic without expanding it (ch60:37).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:33:The crew reaches the wall thirteenth, then tenth, then eleventh; Pike's final book has nine lines, leaves the rating blank, and the cloth still says eleventh (ch7:183–229; ch25:3–49; ch45:105–165; ch59:175–217; ch60:29–31). Brom recovers five bolts from the Ring while the sixth remains on its floor (ch34:113–151; ch35:15–23). The sheet count closes at eleven Ring, twenty-nine Stair and twelve Hall, fifty-two total (ch57:13–17; ch60:19–25).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:39:Cael's calf reopens on mountain and Ring and closes by day 99; his ribs are retaped, later billed by the Hall, cold-aggravated, and quiet by day 129 (ch19:151–159; ch20:27–35; ch34:149–177; ch35:265–271; ch54:139–175; ch55:89–103; ch59:19–21, :47–49). Brom's one hand has four finger-pad cuts, his right shoulder takes the bolt and then the Hall reopening, and every treatment carries forward (ch34:113–151; ch49:237–273; ch51:125–153; ch54:139–175; ch55:25–45; ch56:33–67). Karis's hand and throat remain impaired until their staged recoveries; her mountain emptying is reserve exhaustion, not an untracked wound (ch19:125–173; ch20:41–53; ch34:113–137; ch35:241–251). Oryn's reserve is repeatedly priced and is full again only after three days without mending (ch34:179–225; ch47:43–85; ch51:125–153; ch60:109–119).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:49:The first and second poles are exact at ch7:289 and ch44:219. `Don't declare anything` appears in its original form at ch5:169. Oryn's river-in-the-dark rule is intact at ch22:73. The covenant occupies ch36:201–225 and its final distinction is exact at ch36:217. Oryn's route condition is intact at ch47:201. The Ring and Stair `Later` exchanges match exactly at ch33:257–261 and ch50:205–209. Pike's documents and spoken ledger lines remain exact at their mapped positions (ch3:253–261; ch7:27–47; ch24:119–179; ch45:105–165; ch59:161–207).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:51:No protected unnamed role gains a name: Teague's people remain spear/bow/boy/healer; Thornwater's household, the carters, the six on the rim and the fourth site remain unnamed (ch7:301–345; ch22:159–173; ch49:21–83; ch56:19–25; ch58:117–139). Spoken and written fragment lists use `the Bronze from Ardenmere` rather than Feryn beside Oryn (ch38:23–25; ch60:37).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:59:The book uses `[UNBOUND]` once, and only as a dating limit (ch42:269). `Compact` is spoken in the authorized stake discussion and later protected/book-ending contexts, not as early public knowledge (ch34:247–249; ch58:229; ch60:83). Oryn learns the fragment mechanism from Cael's telling, with sources identified by Path or protected description; no outsider tells her (ch38:3–47). Teague is neither read nor told; his wrist remains his information (ch56:153–205).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:61:Karis's hypothesis is acknowledged and never stated, including in her private exchange with Cael (ch43:57–111; ch44:61). `The still place` remains Cael's private label until Oryn is told, and the crew hears it only afterward (ch55:193–203, :243–279; ch57:191–211). It is not presented as newly discovered at the ending (ch60:39). Nothing explains why the fragments answer inside a Quieting; the strongest statement remains `I don't know why` (ch38:25–31; ch60:261–265).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:67:The thread meets the Reader Standard without qualification. Before the taking, Cael states that Oryn cannot consent, admits that his real motive for silence is fear of her refusal, hears four people distinguish permission to read him from permission to take from her, and writes that he has chosen her cost (ch36:65–225). In the act, he knows that stopping is the right road and reaches anyway (ch37:141–171). The text neither excuses the choice nor disguises it as a misunderstanding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:69:Oryn then names the wrong precisely: he took her asking, reversed the terms of her table, and cannot appoint his own punishment or forgiveness (ch38:103–229). His new rule is not merely `ask`; Oryn adds purpose, forbidding him to use a willing body just to see whether he can (ch39:281–291; ch44:145–213).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:79:1. **Hands — 1,508 occurrences (687 in ch1–30; 821 in ch31–60).** Hands are the book's moral and practical image—work, reading, healing, taking, restraint—but they become the default stage business too (ch1:39–67; ch33:91–119; ch48:17–23; ch56:153–205). Preserve bodily-consent and craft uses; thin neutral placement and handling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:81:3. **`That was` explanatory codas — 334 (155/179).** The narration often gives an image or statement and then interprets it through `That was...` (ch1:63; ch15:57–71; ch38:223–225; ch55:179). This is the most audible new sentence move across movement boundaries.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:83:5. **Accounting lexicon — enter-family 112, price-family 105, cost/bill-family 147.** The ledger language is the novel's design, yet it spreads beyond logs into ordinary thought and gesture (ch4:91–109, :183; ch34:23; ch46:259–285; ch55:275–287). Keep actual logs, contracts and costs; thin metaphorical bookkeeping where the scene already shows the price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:85:7. **`As if / as though` — 90 (52/38).** Many comparisons clarify unfamiliar work, but the same hinge also explains faces and silences that could stand unaided (ch2:149–183; ch37:33–61; ch50:293).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:90:The Book 6 watch list is much improved. Exact `squared` occurs twice; quarter-turns do not occur; `for a moment/while` plus `after a while` occurs eleven times; `did not look` four; `nobody said` three; `did not ask` eight; `He found that` four; and the approximate `not X but Y` pool is nineteen. Exact `flat` appears 111 times, but the great majority are literal terrain, a flat-footed gait, a flat hand or site geometry rather than the old voice tic (ch1:77–109; ch23:133–163; ch29:155–165). `Let it stand` occurs eight times and `put/set it by` eight; those are smaller but audible shared habits (ch10:285; ch45:165; ch55:179; ch60:255).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:98:M4 turns `nobody reads me` into a dangerous exception. Five Arbiters stop together; Cael's fragments do not; he conceals that fact from the group (ch27:181–239; ch29:243–309). M5 gives the exception its triumph and moral failure in the same movement: it saves the party at the Ring and enables the non-consensual taking from Oryn (ch31:211–289; ch32:139–301; ch36:65–225; ch37:141–240). M6 converts guilt into a rule and evidence into restraint rather than theory (ch38:103–229; ch41:43–95; ch43:57–111; ch44:145–219). M7 tests the rule under refusal and consent, then weaponizes the Quieting at the Stair (ch47:97–129; ch48:7–105; ch49:21–121; ch50:143–295). M8 makes the exceptional power cooperative rather than solitary and closes on orientation, not explanation (ch54:191–323; ch55:221–287; ch60:247–265).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:106:The clearest straight-read plateau is ch41–43. The term, identical failure, strata, stakes and hypothesis restraint are distinct findings, but the fourth finding begins to feel like a re-proof before the Stair posting restores motion (ch41:163–291; ch42:205–279; ch43:3–111; ch45:177–225). This is a texture/condensation opportunity, not an arc repair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:114:The major long units are intact: Ephram's and Vell's letters (ch26:59–91; ch27:3–39); the covenant (ch36:201–225); the tenth notice (ch37:233–241); Vastin's three-sentence window (ch44:141); the Hall/season ledger line (ch59:187); the final inventory (ch60:35–41); and the exact closing (ch60:255–265). The #48 wording is preserved in the birthday line (ch40:203), Oryn's letter (ch60:223), after-thaw terms (ch59:221; ch60:223), and the final unit (ch60:255–265).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:116:The owner-pending texts stand verbatim and unglossed as instructed: the #49 Path/Quiet log wording (ch27:237–239; ch30:237; ch33:223–273; ch44:219; ch58:229; ch60:255–265), #50 `Six years I've wanted a face` (ch46:111), and #51 `Tomorrow makes three` (ch44:219). They are not findings.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:122:The ford is frightening and exact, not lurid: wounds are shown through lost grip, movement and treatment, with blood used as stakes rather than spectacle (ch10:257–285; ch11:23–57, :209–251, :285–357). The Ring's attack remains spatial and choice-driven even at maximum intensity (ch31:211–289; ch32:3–321). The Stair trap gives the bolt enough anatomy to justify leaving it in, then turns to rescue and healing (ch49:237–273; ch51:125–153). The Hall creature remains alive and the violence is framed as escape, not punishment (ch54:251–303; ch55:153–165). Nothing exceeds the clean-language or non-lurid standard.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:124:No one-pass comprehension failure survives. The densest passage is the five-finding sequence in ch41–43, but Karis's distinction between what is seen and what is feared is clear (ch43:57–111). The consent sequence is clearer still and never asks a young reader to infer whether the taking was wrong (ch36:65–225; ch38:103–229).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:137:## 9. Line fixes
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:145:1. **Thin retrospective interpretation.** Search all 334 `that was` occurrences and 315 `as [subject] had` comparisons. In lane A (ch1–30), revise or remove **35–45** instances, concentrating on ch15–22 and ch27–30. In lane B (ch31–60), revise or remove **50–60**, concentrating on ch38–43 and ch54–60. Let the current object, changed body or spoken finding carry the meaning; when a callback is necessary, keep one concrete shared detail rather than replaying the earlier scene's interpretation. Leave protected logs, explicit injury clocks and cause-critical comparisons alone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:153:Chapters at 6% skeleton or above were ch25 (9%), ch26 (7%), ch33 (6%), ch34 (10%), ch36 (12%), ch37 (8%), ch44 (8%), ch46 (6%), ch52 (6%), ch58 (6%) and ch60 (9%). Each was checked side by side against the source chapters named for its movement: source ch8–10, ch11–13, ch14–16, ch17–20 and ch21–24 respectively.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:162:- manuscript ch34:129 / source ch12:67, **near-verbatim, excluded**: the registered Brom-hand treatment unit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:164:- manuscript ch37:61 / source ch13:171, **near-verbatim, excluded**: Oryn's registered banks/current report.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:165:- manuscript ch44:141 / source ch16:155, **near-verbatim, excluded**: the protected three-sentence Vastin window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:171:For the non-protected prose around those anchors, the edition changes viewpoint, scene entry, physical causation and local beat order. The previous source-shaped procedure around Brom's hand/Calf sequence is now broken by result-first staging and Lira forcing the read (ch34:113–177 versus source ch12:49–95); the Stair chamber now enters through the wrong flame and distributes cold, smell and catalogue across characters (ch52:61–137 versus source ch20:21–45). Those are genuinely new tellings. No source-distance repair is recommended.
