editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:11658:2. **"The still place" is already in the edition's Books 5 and 6.** Cael's logs there call the anomaly "the still place from session nine" (Book 5 ch1, ch45, ch60) and "the still place I don't count" (Book 6 ch34). Book 7's map says the phrase arrives in Movement 8. I followed the packet: this movement never uses it ("something there that did not flow"; "a place in the middle of himself"). The series needs one answer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/audit-notes.md:3:- **Three `[[TIER-B: …]]` markers**: ch38:181 (the packet's "You're the colour of the wall…", after Oryn's condition), ch39:275 (Cael's answer to "Where is it loudest.": "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer."), ch44:105 (Oryn's "North in the morning…", before the whole "Don't go in without me…"). For each, find the unit's FULL wording in the source and supply it as an exact line fix replacing the whole marker line (old = the marker line exactly as it stands; new = the protected text with only the edition's mandatory changes: no named seasons or months, no metric units, no year count since Kindling, edition names). State who speaks and to whom, and give further exact fixes for the joins if the surrounding lines disagree with the restored text or repeat its content.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/audit-notes.md:5:- **"The still place" (flag 2).** The packet says the phrase is not used here ("a place that does not flow") and arrives in Movement 8. But the LOCKED edition already uses "the still place from session nine" as Cael's log name for the anomaly (Book 5 ch1:121, ch45:31, ch60:25; Book 6 ch34:229). Rule what Book 7 should do so the edition is consistent with itself: is avoiding the phrase through Movement 7 workable, and what exactly should Movement 8's beat be (the name for an unknown becoming a LOCATION, read and told) given the phrase is not new to the reader? Give the wording for a coordinator note to Movements 7 and 8, and any fix needed in this movement (the three standing words "Still open. Still real. Patience." are retired here, with the reason).
