editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1677:     5	**REPAIR — fourteen line fixes in chapters 38–44, followed by owner/coordinator resolution of two protected-text/calendar conflicts.** The telling, birthday, integration, five findings, shooting arc, mule transfer, debt, deployment count, bodies, money, and withheld truths otherwise ratify. The two unresolved conflicts are protected *Tomorrow makes three* at dawn on day 111 versus the next actual Quieting entry on day 114 (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:215–217`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26–33`), and the restored protected promise that Oryn will be “three days north” when the crew is back at the board versus Lowmarch on day 112 and Oryn at Millrace, south of Lowmarch, on day 113 (`source chapter-16.md:127`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:38–40,55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20,26,30`). Neither may be repaired by altering protected wording.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1698:    26	2. **The still place — KEEP this movement’s avoidance; AMEND the M7/M8 coordination.** Locked Books 5–6 already call the anomaly “the still place from session nine” or “the still place I don’t count” (`book-05 manuscript/chapter-01.md:121`; `chapter-45.md:31`; `chapter-60.md:25`; `book-06 manuscript/chapter-34.md:229`). Avoiding the phrase through M7 remains workable because Cael owes the finding to Oryn and has not made it shared speech (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:167–209`). M8’s novelty is location and disclosure, not coinage (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22,29`). Binding note proposed for M7 and M8: **“[Coordinator note — still-place continuity, binding.] ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.”** The protected standing words are properly retired here because the anomaly has changed from unseen/unlocatable to locatable and repeatable; observation replaces patience (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:353–373`; `BOOK_MAP.md:285`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1703:    31	7. **North/Millrace — OWNER after protected restoration.** The northern wicket and later west/south bend are locally plausible (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:213–223,295–301`), but the full protected unit says she will be three days north when the crew returns to the board (`source chapter-16.md:127`). The crew is back at Lowmarch day 112 and Oryn is at Millrace, one day south of Lowmarch, day 113 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:38–40,55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26,30`). A road bend cannot reconcile those assertions.
