50:- **PASS: days 96–100 with no drift.** Chapters 31–33 cover dusk/night of day 96 (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:3-5`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:193`). Chapter 34 explicitly turns the 96th into the 97th and carries the noon mendings (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:3,111-197`). Chapter 35 moves through the night of the 97th, dawn/day 98, and noon/evening 99 (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:63,119,155,265-339`). Chapters 36–37 are the night before and first light of day 100 (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:201-227,229-275`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:1-5`). This matches the packet (`MOVEMENT-005.md:7`) and the ledger's day-96 close (`STATE_LEDGER.md:480-485`).
51-- **Body clocks agree.** Ribs broken on day 78 and untaped on day 99 are twenty-one days, with eighteen days actually taped (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:309-325`; `BOOK_MAP.md:222`). The calf opens day 96 and is closed day 99—“four days, counting the one it went on” (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:265-329`). Brom's string ban runs from day 97 through the first allowable day 100 (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:139-143`). Cael is whole on the 99th, so first light on the 100th is the first day Oryn's own rule permits the long reading (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:321-339`).
