editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-38.md:263:"He told me. All of it, I think; I'd say he doesn't know how to tell less." Oryn looked at the sling, and at the knot on it, which was her own. "It's a true page. You can say I said so. And you can say that true isn't the same as paid."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈27,300. **Oryn cutaway ≈2,000** (day 100, the stool after the telling, the covenant page on her knee; what a healer does with having been a source; no theory). **Karis cutaway ≈2,600** (the week of tables: the tally of kinds she will not say; *the Quieting* chosen because it is the right grammar; **the pen held over the page, and the hypothesis never stated**). **Lira cutaway ≈2,000** (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow someone else spans). **Vastin ≈300** (the courtesy copy; three sentences, substance exact). **Oryn cutaway ≈1,800** (dawn on the 111th onward: north out of the gate with a spare rope, having left her mule with the crew; the route, the debt she set, the line she tested; ends before Millrace's table).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:232:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the gate-to-stone distance is a hundred and ten YARDS (Cael paced it at a yard to the stride; Seln's hundred and four longer paces agree with it); the animal "tracked the buckle" and no sense is named anywhere; Pike's Thornwater line is printed once, in chapter 6, and its saying in chapter 7 is narration; the twelve-second doorway hold is recalled at Thornwater's ladder, not in the day-18 inventory. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:246:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze, said once at a fire. Uninjured. Has not lifted his Path since the crossroads fire. Has walked the first hours of eight roads, five out of Lowmarch and three out of Thornwater; on day 49 he says, in one sentence, that he has walked the first part of all five out of Lowmarch. Has the prints and the forty-five-yard line by the white stone in his head, a hundred and ten yards from the gate (a hundred and four of his own paces), and has told nobody. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:304:- **A flint fire is not a declaration (flag):** on the 59th, above the wash, the crew lights its first road fire since the fifth day, on the finding's first sentence. The hold itself stands unchanged. The Thornwater carter sits at it and says that he will not do it alone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:333:**Open threads.** Two hounds gone down the river, logged as open. Why a hundred and ten yards; why dusk. What quiet ground is, and what a road bends round two days east of Thornwater. Lira's question. Hesk's letter and the roof. What Teague will say when they have cost him something. A hold's slip, with a ford in it, due on the oak in the morning.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:356:- **Oryn** is the first healer met past the Line. Tide as taught: contact only; about three serious mendings a day fed and slept, two on a road; cannot heal herself; "Because I cannot mend what I can't read."; the short reading (seconds) and the long one (both hands, all of her, minutes) — healing houses say surface and deep. The stall is named once. She knows NOTHING of fragments, has run no deep reading, records nothing and remembers. Her reading of Cael stopped at five; she said only "a river in the dark" and that it has no side she can find. "More than one" is NOT said (Movement 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:401:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. **One involuntary full burst on the 78th**, when the ledge went (her body travelled about twenty feet; the declaration and its crack crossed the gorge); a second refused, six yards short of shelter. **Right tibia broken on the 78th, set and mended on the 80th: straight, new, to walk within the week and not to be run on for a month.** **Right ankle never mended** ("That's a tape and a season. It'll set."); she asked once, from the mule's back, on the 82nd; she tapes it herself as Oryn taught her and says that she now knows where it is. Her right boot is under the mountain; she is barefoot on that side. She rode Oryn's mule from the shoulder to Oxhollow and has not said the word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:409:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken". **Her sum (her window, the 92nd):** whole on the 99th by the rule, though her hands say sooner; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; her Thornwater stop ends on the 95th; she means to work four days more at Thornwater's table and has put one day on the route, for the reading. She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record. She told Teague on the hill only that she was late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:413:**Objects and money.** **The cart is in the gorge**, with the ferryman's rope, the blankets, the kettle, the canvas and the flour. Three boxes, whole, and Brom's ash wedge beside them; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. Seln's case. Hesk's satchel, with the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and Pike's lines on bark. Karis's lantern, cord, brass straightedge and Hesk's clock. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two marks earned** (62 + Oxhollow 70); **a hundred and sixteen in hand**; **six owed to the smith** for the cart. Pike's slip is in hand, with five strokes and Oxhollow's mark at its foot, to be carried to the plank. The long leaf was unrolled on the keeper's board and paid for there; the text does not say who carries it away, and the keeper is its buyer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:441:- **The line (OWNER-pending #49, default in force).** At the line the five live Arbiters stop at the same step: Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's. Cael's own Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling and nothing in him changes there; his fragments go on answering inside. The protected log entries are word for word (their loose "mine" is his shorthand). Outside them nothing says "his Path", nothing says his Arbiter is awake or unaffected, and nothing says WHY the fragments answer. The word *Quieting* has not been said. "Compact" has not been said aloud: the stake carries the registry stamp. "Made" has been said of the place once, by Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:449:- **Objects and money:** Oxhollow's grain cart carried the boxes days 85–93; the ferryman's rope is owed in kind, unpriced; the purse ran 116 → 114 → 108; Seln's locked case is shut on his strap throughout (continuity beat added in repair). Letters: Ephram's says "Bracken" (he); Vell's carries "The session still stands," unexplained.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:456:- **Oxhollow's grain cart (flag).** Since his carts "go round", the keeper sends one to Thornwater for grain on the 85th, eight days out and eight home. Its carter is his sister's son: a long, sleepy-faced young man with very large feet and two grey mules, who says about forty words in six days. The three boxes ride his bed from Oxhollow to Thornwater (85th–93rd) for nothing, because the five walk his road in front of him. No paper, no line. He rests the 91st at Lowmarch and loads grain at Thornwater on the 94th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:468:- **The registry's printed sheet (flag):** east of the Line it shows a river or two without their bends, hills drawn alike, and seven dashed roads with no names that run out into white and stop; the third from the top crosses the first water (no ferry, no Lowmarch) and ends three fingers east of it, at about Thornwater's fence or an hour beyond. **"Void"** (flag): Seln says that in a registry's usage an entry is void when nothing is written against it, and supposes that a carter was once shown such a sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:470:- **Oryn at Thornwater (flag):** she mends the carter's split palm on a plank inside the west gate before she eats ("That's one."). Her changed plan: she had meant to sit at this gate's table until the 99th; she walks the Fallow road in those days, the same six gates waiting the same days; Thornwater's bench "goes short" and is to be paid on her way back. She has been round the ring "thirty times, with the mule, by the ruts" (her round goes on east by that road). The carters' saying, as given: *You'll not want her in the ring; she's no good there.*, first heard at the first gate she ever mended at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:540:- **Inside the line** no companion Path was used: Oryn's hands had nothing ("Nothing in my hands"); cloth and knees. Nobody has theorized why the fragments answered. *Quieting* has still not been said. "Compact" has been said aloud once, by Seln. Nothing is known of where the file is, what it says or why; dating stops at "five years… maybe six". Seln's map memory (maps with holes) is open; he asked for the carter's map.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:554:- **Oryn's crossbow (flag):** has an iron stirrup at its nose and is spanned with a hook, which was in the near-side pannier and was not fetched; drawn by hand it cuts the fingers. It "throws low, a hand" at thirteen feet. A leather sleeve on the stock held **six** bolts. No history of the bow is given; Oryn says only that she looked at it at noon and left it, "a healer's reason".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:559:- **Oryn's rule for the long reading:** unfed, at first light, the door shut; the patient on his back with his head at the stool; a surface count first "so that I'd know I hadn't dreamed it"; her left hand under the nape and her right flat on the breastbone; she talks, "to keep my place". She says twenty minutes beforehand, "near enough".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:595:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five. Oryn knows that he can do, inside a line, what no Path can; she saw Wind, a light, and heard an edge ring; she did not see the Shadow use and cannot attribute his arrival at Karis. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln saw it. All six know that the registry's iron stands on the line, that maps were drawn with a blank there, and that the posting was a question which their coming out has answered. Nobody knows where the file is, what it says, or why. Nobody has said why the fragments answer inside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:744:- **The tenth on another person (flag; changed in repair r1).** He asks twice on the 113th, and they are two questions: at Millrace he asks the healer, at her own bench, with her line waiting, and is refused; on the road she offers, as "a woman on a rock" who can say yes (her protected line: "the same day as the lean-to and a different question"). **The short reading is done with one hand**, his right on her wrist (inside upward, broad and brown, a white scar across the heel of the hand): the going-out leaves that hand and is back under his palm almost before he has counted; at three there are banks, "close… and high", and by ten he knows the Path "as a friend's step on a stair" is known. For the minute she has him put his left hand on the back of her neck as well: one channel, one thing in it, which does not wander or pool, and leans to meet whatever touches it. Bill to him: the reading hand slow for an hour, and hunger.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:751:- **The brass on the hide:** she strikes out *guess* beside the ring a day south of Lowmarch, and says that she is going to find out how far wrong a map of days can be along one line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:764:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. **Right shoulder: bolted through from behind on the 114th, mended once that night; the arm bound across his chest; nothing on that side until Oryn says.** He carried the kit up forty steps on the left. He has the healer's bow again, its hook, and **five bolts**. He has quoted Rooke. He lays six bowls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:770:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. **On the round's terms, as a stop:** "when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me"; she goes when the round cannot spare her. Nineteen days late at the ford with the oxen by her own sum, "or more"; word sent north by a carter, with where to send for the child. Five mendings in two days (three at Millrace; Brom and Lira at the stone). She refused him at her own bench and offered on the road, the same day ("a different question"). She has been read by him once, short (one hand on her wrist) and long, and has been told what he found in her. She has not forgiven him, and has not been told what he found in himself. She does not know where the ninth came from. Her pannier and rope are on the grey jenny.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:788:- **Bills and bodies:** Cael's right forearm bends but carries Compression's blow, and his left palm is taped with an unmended weal; Lira's reopened marks are shut and the sling is shorter, but the no-hold order and taped/unmended ankle stand; Brom's right arm is bound after one shoulder mending and must not be used until Oryn says (51:123–163; 52:5,75).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:796:**Movement 7 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the ten audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed; ch52's three tracked passages restaged (scene 2 re-entered on the bolt at the thirty-first step; the kit read from the cord inward); the design confirmed once; twice-told states removed from ch49–51 with the night log whole; the closing log's "five years ago" made to stand (the ledger's eight stations are the old irons, five cold terms by Seln; the stroke-and-bar is "two visits", the later undated; nothing decoded); a register pass. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — seven applied by the coordinator: **what Cael asked at Millrace's bench is corrected to the source's actual distinction** (leave to touch a boy's wrist while Oryn held it — refused; on the road he asks to read HER — granted, "a different question"), with the bench's count and the day's log to match; and ch52 says Karis reads the radius figure from scaled divisions within the lone line, not as a spacing along the wall. All three tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap as below. 42413 words (the length ruled by the coordinator: the Stair's action not cut for the map's 40,000 line). Author-sourced sections above refreshed from the post-repair report; where they still describe the bench request as a request to read Oryn, the Tide ruling above governs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:806:- **Teague is neither read nor asked** and knows nothing of the mechanism. He forfeited the four-mark weir slip to come (it was never set or paid); the axe-head hold's fence (forty) passes to the five for the cold term ("Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / "Ours,"); "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew is unnamed, the older healer of no Path included.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:811:- **Bodies:** Lira's left arm slung and holding nothing, her right ankle never mended; her order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"); Oryn's crossbow is with Lira with ONE bolt left. Brom's shoulder opened, was mended a second time and is BOUND, not mended a third ("It will not hold three times this season"). Cael's three old ribs took Compression again (ten days; quiet on the 129th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:853:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst in this movement. **Left arm slung high, all eight marks taken (read by Oryn at the fork on the 122nd), still under the order: it holds nothing until Oryn says, and she has not said; five weeks on the 131st.** It took no part in her two shots in the Hall, and it held nothing in a fall on the ice on the 127th. **Right ankle taped, never mended**; she walks on the whole sole; Oryn left her a roll at the fork. **She carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap, spanned, with one bolt in it**; she cannot span it; she shot it twice in the Hall, one-handed, and hit twice. She has not asked for the ankle again. She has not crossed, touched or tried the fourth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:861:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. At Thornwater, "on the route". **She has been paid what she set**: three readings, and all of it told, with his hand on her wrist; she has said "It's paid." **She has not forgiven him, and the answer that she kept is still kept.** Her finding stands: she has never felt such a thing in anyone, and does not know what right would look like in him. She has no theory and has been offered none. She knows the mechanism, and the nine by Path. She has the mill's grey jenny, her pannier and rope. Her own brown mule is with the crew. She was three weeks late at the ford with the oxen on the 125th. The old woman's knee, mended at Millrace on the 113th, has held. Her letter: *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:887:- **Lira:** left arm slung high, eight marks taken, holding nothing until Oryn says; right ankle taped and never mended; Oryn's spanned crossbow on its strap with one bolt, and Lira cannot span it (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:17-27`; `manuscript/chapter-59.md:25-37`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:231-237`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:895:- **Letters:** Hesk's parcel/straightedge arrived; Cael sent Hesk and Vell replies west, including Vell's “session still stands”; Ephram remains unanswered but is promised the first thaw boat; Oryn's exact bark letter is carried in Hesk's satchel and needs no answer (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:59-89,213-227`). The clerk's packet says only that the crew kept the kit (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:87-89`). OWNER #25's Lira-family line remains opaque and receives no new setup.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:23:- **Pike says the Fallow line before the door is shut;** it costs a line (eleventh; "Teague's ten up"). Then what the wall cannot say: thirty years, forty-odd crews, nobody over a line and back, "Six in and six out, and the sixth a healer." **The room updates** without a word (the hide-woman, the crew of three gone grey, the carter from the first week, the boy). **Teague stands** when they come in and sits at "eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty meters**: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Anchor let off at ten meters as perception, then as a hand: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,200. **Lira cutaway ≈1,800** (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose before she did; "That was me. The loud thing."). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,600** (days 84–92: out of Oxhollow's gate north on her route, the carter's hand she owed, the child three stops on, the patient she wants to read whole; she decides to put a day on the route; it ends before Thornwater). **Teague cutaway ≈1,400** (day 84, Oxhollow's ford at dusk: four sentences priced before he says them).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:30:- **Oxhollow (day 84):** the table under the lean-to, hers twenty days at a time; worst first; "That's three." The map paid seventy ("Then they go round."). **The second and third readings** (ribs knitting with "nothing doing it"; the wrist and neck, nothing wrong, still nothing): "a river in the dark." **The two readings taught before they are load-bearing** (surface: a count of ten; deep: both hands, minutes, still and whole, at a mending's cost; "I don't run it on a road"). If the stall is named (C8 default: at most once), it is a limit she prices and hates, never used. **Three questions** (right places — yes; faster; no healer ever got anything — no). "That's the visit." He has a sentence asking her south and does not say it. "Thornwater's on my route in nine days… I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:41:  **Win sentence, verbatim.** Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's week of colours.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:32:  - The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge. **The young one goes out a stride to drag him and is killed by the sixth volley.** Oryn's hands are on him, and come off with nothing done. Vastin cannot move. The broad man says the name, once. [OWNER-pending #54]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:42:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "After the next thaw … My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Oryn: "The day I have to." … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:54:- The death is brief and not graphic. Its cost carries: eleven, the gap where a fourth stood, and Teague one short and not saying the number. Nobody strikes a retreating opponent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-27.md:111:"The holds either side won't put a beast on it," said Oryn. "I've asked. They don't give you a reason. They say it's fallow, as you'd say a field was resting, and then they talk about something else."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The winter fence** given over ("Ours."). Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "Spring." **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:41:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:75:It was only three words. But it had not come out as her other sentences came, each one finished and set down like a bowl on a board; the middle of it had given a little under her, as a plate gives underfoot. He made no answer, since he did not think that she could have borne to be answered. She had told a mill that she would be nobody's sixth, and a board at Thornwater that she was a stop; she had eaten out of their bowl for a week, standing; and this was the only way that she had of saying what a person became to her when she had gone into a marsh after his friend and watched him go into worse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:32:- **The silent yard** (two or three bouts across the cold term, ~1,500 each) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19]. Teague's crew and the five spar in the frozen meadow with steel and bodies, and no Paths. Cael loses to the tall woman's spear reach, then makes a visible correction. She never says a word to any of the five. Lira coaches from the bench, one-armed. The rival clock appears on the page. Teague is the better field captain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:23:- **Lowmarch, day 90:** two hold slips with HOLD and **five names** ("Holds came to the ferry. Asked who. I said you."), waiting a fortnight or Teague. The traverse line read and priced: "Sixty-four's what the job was worth." / "Fair." **The posting under the stone's far edge**, the dust-curve on it, the hook-and-bar seal in wax; he reads it upside down, then gives it to Pike. Pike's face stops; Cael counts nine. "That's the Fallow Ring." / "That's quiet ground." **Pike's speech** (protected) and "You'll know. Your Arbiter tells you. It stops." Karis brings the page with two lines under it from the middle box: "A location. And a contract." The smith paid: a hundred and eight. Lira at the roof's edge: "Two hundred times. He counted." / "So do you. I've never once heard you say never."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:- **The board's room:** the wall rewritten, tenth; "Teague's nine up… He read that slip yesterday. Read it twice… I'd have done the same, and I told him, and he said he knew." **The council, once, in order:** Karis's case; Brom ("A survey kit's a cart's worth… That's not the reason. That's what it is."); Lira ("I'm saying it's a walk and a carry. I'm not saying it isn't the other thing."); Cael: "It pays."; **Seln reads the paper, not the words**: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside." / "It goes in." / "That's not a reason not to go." **The ninety-third**: nobody says *bring her*, and Karis writes "Thornwater, ninety-third. The healer." The Part-1 summary log (protected, "Twelve weeks").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:27:- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:24:- **C1 (default unless the owner rules otherwise):** in Lowmarch's first week the horse and cart are sold. A horse is fodder and a sign that says *paper*; the scrub ruts past Lowmarch take mules. The sale and what is left of the Book 6 purse become a sealed reserve that Brom's rule keeps them from living on. The log's "in hand" counts only what the board pays. Give it one good scene and an argument with a joke in it, then let it go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:28:- **The Thornwater road (days 41–43), ≈4,000:** the carter at the fire ("Two carts went quiet on it last month"); the stretch at dusk after a wheel cost an hour; positions; the valley's noise; **Lira's hand up at a hole in the noise**; Seln without turning, "Don't declare anything." / "Walk. Same pace."; "I could clear it." / "No." / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it."; Brom becoming exactly as large as his body and no larger; Karis deciding five times not to take out the notebook; the five items (keeps station at forty meters; makes no sound; tracks the buckle; won't cross the gravel fan; reacts to nothing because they gave it nothing); it stops a hundred meters short of the fence. No blow struck.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:30:- **Lowmarch, day 49 — the board anatomized:** a woman captain's line read before and after; the eleven-bale captain ("Say it again and I'll write it"); "The book's for me. The saying's for them."; the wall at the lower inn; "A Bronze who lost my carter…"; "Did you ever hear of a ledger-keeper called Vell?" / "No."; Seln's finger on the carter's map, the asset-restriction **said once and put away**, the map turned east. "Four lines. Nobody lost, nobody hurt, nobody knows you." Brom: "Eleven."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:73:*Sixtieth day. Lowmarch. A letter from Hesk, with nothing on the outside but my name and "past the Line". It found me because there is only the one board. He writes that my grandmother crossed the Line once, before I was born. It is the first I have heard that I had one. I don't know her name. I have set down what the letter says, and nothing that I might guess.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-34.md:175:"No." Oryn let go of him, and wiped her hands on her breeches. "And I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-51.md:303:"No," said Teague. "It isn't. I've none to give you. If any one of you would sooner set stakes tomorrow and go home, he can say so now, and I'll think no worse of him."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-43.md:129:"All eight. That last one's caught up with the others. It was slow, and it isn't slow now." Oryn drew the wool up and tied it. "That changes nothing that I said at the stone. You've a fortnight behind you, and the rest to do. Nothing in that hand till I say."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:17:It is the 270th day at Lowmarch. There are six now, with Oryn's spring stop at Pike's plank. Lira has two arms she does not quite trust, and Brom's shoulder is still bound and unread. The ferryman says the ice will go in a week, and has said so for a week. Karis's case is made and no one has answered it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:28:- **The long table** (midday). The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, verbatim; these are their first words to each other. Vastin says the short thing: he resigned or walked out. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence ("Under every station on the continent. I said so at a table in the autumn"). Vastin's new fact: "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail ends at Treswick. Vastin then has nothing to do. Lira asks "Why us." Oryn notices the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that crosses the Line, and the Stair's rim "is not mine". Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only, "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks. **Close (verbatim).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43:- "Noted" order: Vastin's first is here. Teague does not say it yet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md:93:There were more than six. Teague had come down off the rise with the first of the light to say that he was going, and he stood a little outside the ring of them, with his thumbs in his belt, as a man stands at a neighbour's fence. Karis did not seem to mind him. She had the hide flat under four pebbles, and the three rings on it, and Cael saw that the third was not where it had been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md:121:"Three days out along it," he said. "No farther. If there's nothing under the brass by the third dusk, we turn for Lowmarch, and I'll say so then without anybody having to ask me."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:38:  **Win sentence, verbatim.** Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's week of colours.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:33:- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:61:| 6 | Back at Lowmarch: the board anatomized (read before and after; "The book's for me. The saying's for them."); the eleven-bale captain; the wall at the lower inn; "A Bronze who lost my carter…"; Vell asked after; the map turned east (asset-restriction said once); the first pole in the log; Teague read across the room and reading back (Ch2) | 49 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:66:| 11 | Lowmarch: Seln takes the well ("I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report."); Brom asks what the board pays a man with no Path and writes it down; Hesk's letter (the grandmother); the saying; twelfth; "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something." (Ch4) | 60 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:139:**Two hard rules for every window:** (1) **No member of Teague's crew is named, ever**, including in Teague's own head. Book 8 kills "the young one" at the pass and says his name once without entering it. Teague thinks of his people as the spear, the bow, the boy and the healer, which is how a captain counts. (2) **Oryn's holds stay unnamed** except Oxhollow, Thornwater and Millrace. In her head they are what they owe her or what is there: the hold with the child; the hold that gave the coat; the fourth, four days on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Seln** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M1: 1,800 (days 10–40: walking every road out of Lowmarch, and later Thornwater, alone; the report nobody asks for) · M5: 2,000 (day 97, at the stone, then the stake: the maps with holes unlocking; ends as he asks for the carter's map) · M7: 2,200 (night of day 112: the second slip held against the first in his head; six years carrying a case; wanting a face) · M8: 1,600 (days 124–128: the ledger in his coat on the road home; giving it to Karis) | His fifteen years; the maps he carried and their blanks; the registry's form-prose; the case's known contents (the machine's maintenance records, read in B6); his read of the trap; his anger | Where the Quieting file is or what it says ("I carried the maps. I never saw the file."); any face or name on the rim; the case opened; the index decoded; the stroke-and-bar decoded; any sentence of affection said aloud |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's spring term (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:269:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:283:- Ch13, the covenant, whole: *Written before. Tomorrow morning, the back room, the door shut. Oryn runs the long reading. Both hands, all of her, all of me, twenty minutes. I lie still. I'm still and whole for the first time in front of her; she said so in the yard, with the tape off.* / *The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.* / *The price. She doesn't know what I am. She can't consent to what she can't know about — not won't; can't. There's nothing I could put in front of her tonight that she could say yes or no to, because the thing doesn't have a name she's heard. I've decided not to tell her before. My reasons are good, and they're the reasons of somebody who wants it, and the real one is that I don't know what she'd say. Entered.* / *If it takes what she's using on me, it takes it from the one person on this road who came to help. I don't know what it costs a source. It's never shown. Tomorrow's the first time it could, and if it does, she pays, and I chose that for her.* / *After: I tell her. In full. On her table, before I'm off it. Whatever it costs me, including the route walking north without me on it.* / *I want it. Write that too.* / *Write it before, not after. That's the whole difference between me and the system.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:294:- Ch23: *Hundred and twenty-second day, the fork. Oryn north. On her terms. I didn't ask. Five on the bearing.* — *I love this country.* — and the crest: *Four sites. One line. The last one's twice the size and the Compact fenced it. The bearing runs through it and keeps going. Karis says four points is an argument. I say it's a bearing — the kind their maps draw as nothing. Home is Lowmarch now. I just wrote that without noticing. Nineteen, ten fragments, a still place at the center of me, and a line on a map that somebody drew before there were maps. We're not done. We're oriented.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:308:- Ch11: Seln: "The road's cut." … "The grass. Where the cord went." — Oryn: "Move," … "I can't fix this here. Move." … "She keeps it." — **The order:** "A mend that deep holds nothing for a season. Nothing. That arm is not to hold. It's not to strike. It's not to catch. Not a rope, not a knife, not a fall, not a friend. Not until I say. And I'll say at first snow, near enough, if it's let alone." … "One arm. From here to the snow." — "The ankle's a tape and a season. I've told you that before." — Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes," Cael said. / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:310:- Ch13: Oryn: "You don't get a yes. You get told." — Karis: "Ephram fought you in earnest and the notice said non-hostile. This is earnest and it isn't a fight at all." … "The model doesn't say the engagement has to be a fight. It says it has to be real." — Seln: "That's not consent. It's the nearest thing to it the log's ever had, and it's still not it. I'd enter both." — Lira: "She asked to read you," … "She didn't ask for the rest. Those aren't the same sentence." — Oryn's twenty-minute report: "I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read." — "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was." — "Something just changed," she said. "In you. While I was in there." / "Yes." / "Did I do that?" / "No. I did." … "I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it. You've been still for twenty minutes. I want to see if you can manage twenty-one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:315:- Ch18: Oryn: "No." … "You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next." — "You're asking me to break the route," / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." — "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." — **Terms:** "You're on the route now. Which means when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me." — "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it…" — "You're built to arrive." / "Yes," she said. "That's what I am." — Lira: "He asked twice and got one," / Brom: "That's the rate," — Seln: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:317:- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred meters and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it."

